## Firestore Data Model

```
profiles/{userId}          — full user profile, photos[], visibility_settings{}
likes/{likeId}             — { fromUserId, toUserId, likeType: 'heart'|'friendship', matched, createdAt }
passes/{passId}            — { fromUserId, toUserId }
conversations/{convId}     — { participants[], likeType, lastMessage, unreadCount{} }
  messages/{msgId}         — { text, senderId, timestamp, read }
presence/{userId}          — online/offline tracking
```

## Core Conventions

- **Icons** are inline SVGs using `fill="currentColor"` / `stroke="currentColor"` — colour via CSS inheritance
- **`RainbowIcon`** component (defined locally in Likes, Messages, ViewProfile) represents friendship/wave
- **System messages** use `senderId: 'system'` for match/friend notifications in chat
- **Bottom nav** lives inside each page component (Home, Likes, Messages, Chat, Profile). Uses `useUnreadCount()` hook to show orange badge on the messages icon
- **Visibility settings** stored as `visibility_settings: { fieldKey: boolean }` on the profile — `false` = hidden, anything else = visible
- **Deploy command**: `npm run build && firebase deploy --only hosting`
- **`back-arrow-button`** CSS class is reused across ViewProfile, EditPhotos, EditProfile for consistent back navigation
